  "hinge": "The cause is not the arithmetic and it is not the president's metaphor. It is the choice — by Herzog, whether \"innovative ideas\" means a published process or a permission slip; by Eisenkot, whether his \"foundational terms\" are a text or a mood; by the Joint List and Ra'am, whether their recommendation is free or priced; by the opposition, whether the direct-election bill is a remedy for deadlock or a method for excluding a fifth of the electorate from governing; and by Likud, whether the certificate is signed under an evidenced claim or a withdrawn one. §6:148 does not speak about coalitions at all — it says that a people cannot be assessed by the deeds of an individual or a group, which is the precise operation that turned nineteen seats into an accusation of foreign takeover. The ladders are being raised on Wednesday; whether anyone climbs down them is still undecided."
